even a great movie can be ruined by a  bad ending it's arguably the hardest and  most important part to get right  continuity errors and awkward dialogue  might be forgiven but a movies ending  sticks with the audience long after the  credits roll thankfully that's what  alternate endings are for check out  these famous films with awesome  alternate endings but watch out for  spoilers Heather's in the 1988 black  comedy Heather's Veronica played by  Winona Ryder learns a lesson about the  high cost of popularity after she joins  a clique of girls all named Heather at  her school she also becomes romantically  involved with the new student JD played  by Christian Slater who is determined to  shake up the social status quo in some  very unexpected ways like with bombs in  the theatrical ending after JD's bomb  explodes  Veronica walks into the school where she  encounters Heather Duke Veronica takes  away Heather's red scrunchie and tells  her Heather my love there's a new  sheriff in town then she catches up to  her old friend Martha dumptruck gunstock  and the film ends on a hopeful note  several other endings - Heather's were  scrapped along the way the original  ending was the bomb was strapped to me  and I give this amazing speech in the  best alternate version writer Daniel  waters gives Martha dumb stock the last  laugh when Veronica tries to rekindle  their friendship  Martha stabs her in the chest calling  her Heather as she dies Veronica  protests that her name isn't Heather but  Martha ignores her getting up from her  wheelchair and triumphantly walking away  from the friends that betrayed her ouch  the butterfly effect in the 2004  psychological thriller at the butterfly  effect 20-year old Evan discovers his  frequent headaches and blackouts are  actually a manifestation of his ability  to travel back in time  Evan uses his childhood journals to go  back and change traumatic experiences  for himself and his friends however he  soon learns that even small and  seemingly positive changes can  drastically affect the future and not  always in a good way in the theatrical  ending Evan travels back to the day he  met his four  Kaleigh and changes things so they never  meet and become neighbors when evan  returns to the future he's relieved to  see that this change has made things  better for the lives of his friends he  burns his journals thereby preventing  himself from ever altering the timeline  again the alternate ending found on the  director's cut DVD is much darker than  the original on the brink of madness  evan travels back in time strangling  himself in the womb with his own  umbilical cord to prevent his own birth  for a movie that offers so much to think  about this ending is definitely the more  thought-provoking one first blood in the  1982 action film first blood Vietnam  veteran John Rambo drifts through  Washington State where he has a run-in  with an intolerant sheriff after the  former Green Beret refuses to be pushed  around by the authoritarian cop  Rambo finds himself fighting for his  life as he tries to escape the small  town and invade the lawmen and his  lackeys at the end  Rambo corners and wounds the sheriff  preparing to kill him however his former  commander Colonel Sam Troutman arrives  in time to stop John from doing the deed  and Rambo breaks down recounting his  traumatic experiences during the war and  surrendering to Troutman it's not  necessarily a bad ending but it was a  little unsatisfying and it left the door  open for several mediocre sequels the  original ending - first blood keeps much  closer to David morals 1972 novel Rambo  still has his tearful breakdown but he  decides that the events of Vietnam have  made his life all but pointless as he  can't live normally in society anymore  Rambo gives the colonel his gun  when Troutman can't do it  rainbow grabs his arm causing the gun to  go off given what we know of rainbows  character this finale seems like a more  fitting and realistic way for him to go  out pretty and pink John Hughes 1986  cult classic pretty and pink features  geeky high schoolers Andy and her best  friend  ducky ducky is madly in love with Andy  but she begins dating the popular blame  triggering a bitter argument with ducky  later plains friend Steph teases him  about Andy causing Blaine to avoid her  and lie about his prom plans undeterred  Andy goes to the prom alone but she  still has a chance to find true love at  the prom and and ducky make up and head  for the dance floor after telling Steph  what he thinks of him Blaine  congratulate ducky and tells Andy how he  feels about her kissing her on the cheek  and walking out  [Music]  ducky puts his own feelings aside and  encourages Andy to follow him Andy and  Blaine kiss in the parking lot  ducky dances with a cute girl and they  all live happily ever after  it's all very romantic if you're a 13  year old girl test audiences as it turns  out didn't like the original ending  which had Andy choose ducky over plain  pretty and pink should have been about  two geeks finding love but the revised  ending turns into a formulaic teen fairy  tale except Blaine is no Prince Charming  hey let's go upstairs huh jon cryer may  be famous for that dance in the record  store but the scene where ducky sits in  his room listening to Morrissey is the  most honest performance of teenage  heartbreak ever filmed Scott Pilgrim vs.  the world in Edgar rates 2010 action  comedy Scott Pilgrim vs. the world  slacker musician Scott Pilgrim flounders  his way through an unsatisfying life  he's a bassist and a struggling Garage  Band he has no plans for the future and  his girlfriend knives Chow is a clingy  17 year old high school student when  Scott meets Ramona he immediately  becomes infatuated with her but he must  defeat her seven evil exes in order to  win her heart the ending used for the  theatrical release was actually supposed  to be the movies alternate ending it was  shot after the original one had been  filmed in order to match the ending of  the Scott Pilgrim graphic novels after  helping Scott defeat Ramona's final evil  ex knives tells Scott that she's come to  terms with their breakup and understands  that their relationship is over although  she swore to win him back  knives gives her blessing for Scott to  pursue his new romance with Ramona in  the film's original ending Scott  realizes that he still has feelings for  knives your hair is getting really  shaggy it is  I like it  you do the cup will rekindle their  romance over a videogame and Ramona  realizes that she doesn't need to be in  a relationship or constantly reinventing  herself to be happy staying healthy and  mature decision making in a movie is  like seeing a unicorn in the wild which  is why we love this ending die hard with  a vengeance in 1995's die hard with a  vengeance terrorists  Simon Gruber has taken all of New York  City hostage in order to steal a  boatload of gold and to get revenge on  lieutenant John McClane for the death of  his brother Hans with the help of Harlem  shopkeepers Zeus Carver McClane deals  with the bomb threats in bank heists as  he pursues Gruber and his lackeys across  the five boroughs at the film's climax  McClane follows Gruber to a hideout in  Quebec most of the bad guys are quickly  rounded up but Gruber and his girlfriend  attempt to escape in a helicopter  McClane manages to get the best of them  it's a typical action film finale  unrealistic full of questionable physics  and made to showcase a big explosion  because in an alternate ending Gruber  escapes with the gold while McClane  takes the blame for the terrorists trail  of destruction  the NYPD kicks McClane off the force but  he goes rogue and tracks down Simon  Gruber himself how are my friends and  the NYPD well I was fired from the NYPD  cops trying to save my pension oh I'm  sorry to hear that  he corners the villain forcing him to  play a game of McClane says with riddles  and a rocket launcher thrown in for fun  after a few suspenseful rounds Gruber  loses taking an RPG to the chest this  more realistic ending is miles better  than the theatrical version sometimes a  small boom is even more satisfying than  a big one  [Music]
 

